      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, it is not wrong to feel like the story is ending; that ending you sense might actually be a necessary \"void\" to make room for something that doesn't rely on the \"holy grail\" to give you meaning.\n\nThe exhaustion you feel is your life finally taking a breath after the decade of holding its breath for us to find a way to stop \"running\" and start \"living.\"\n\nThe \"blank pages\" at the end of the book often become the most important parts of the life we can finally write with no one to tell the \"what next.\"",
